  "reasoning": "Cook Political Report\u2019s statewide Partisan Voting Index lists Kentucky as R+15, indicating a strongly Republican structural advantage in federal elections.[1][5] In the most recent presidential baseline cited, Donald Trump carried Kentucky by roughly 62.5% to 46.1% combined for his main opponents (a margin of about 16.4 points), and the state has not voted for a Democratic presidential nominee since 1996, underscoring a durable Republican advantage in federal-level contests.[7][18] With no recent (last 45 days) head\u2011to\u2011head federal polling located and Kentucky\u2019s registration and recent voting patterns continuing to favor Republicans, the best current assessment is that Kentucky leans clearly Republican for federal races, using those prior federal results as the margin benchmark.[3][19]",
